1
00:00:13,993 --> 00:00:17,038
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:38,726 --> 00:00:39,561
What was that?

3
00:00:41,813 --> 00:00:42,814
Why are you flustered?

4
00:00:42,897 --> 00:00:45,692
Two years of living together,
and a kiss shocks you?

5
00:00:45,775 --> 00:00:47,986
-It was out of nowhere.
-What is this, a drama?

6
00:00:48,069 --> 00:00:49,404
Should I have set the mood?

7
00:00:51,531 --> 00:00:54,325
I got you, didn't I?
You're not my boyfriend.

8
00:00:54,409 --> 00:00:55,410
Now, fess up.

9
00:00:55,493 --> 00:00:57,078
Tell me who I really am

10
00:00:57,162 --> 00:00:58,329
and who you are.

11
00:00:58,413 --> 00:01:00,665
You're sure I'm not your boyfriend
after one kiss?

12
00:01:00,748 --> 00:01:04,169
If kissing a girl like me flusters you,
it's one of two things.

13
00:01:05,086 --> 00:01:07,297
Either you're not my boyfriend,

14
00:01:08,381 --> 00:01:09,215
or you're gay.

15
00:01:09,299 --> 00:01:10,550
I'm not.

16
00:01:11,801 --> 00:01:13,678
-You want to make that clear?
-Enough.

17
00:01:13,761 --> 00:01:14,846
Don't do that again.

18
00:01:15,430 --> 00:01:16,806
Just as I'm unfamiliar to you,

19
00:01:16,890 --> 00:01:19,642
I also find my girlfriend,
who's forgotten me, unfamiliar.

20
00:01:23,521 --> 00:01:25,273
Eat that and take your meds.

21
00:01:29,235 --> 00:01:30,570
I'm absolutely certain.

22
00:01:30,653 --> 00:01:33,114
How is this
what two years together looks like?

23
00:01:39,204 --> 00:01:40,663
Sheesh, that woman…

24
00:01:45,793 --> 00:01:46,628
Eel?

25
00:01:47,378 --> 00:01:48,963
Goodness me.

26
00:01:49,464 --> 00:01:51,174
I could've just eaten at home.

27
00:01:51,257 --> 00:01:53,885
Why'd you bring a late-night snack
all the way here?

28
00:01:54,385 --> 00:01:57,263
You'd be hungry by the time you got home.

29
00:01:57,347 --> 00:01:58,640
Oh boy.

30
00:01:58,723 --> 00:02:02,352
And today's the day we finally open this.

31
00:02:02,936 --> 00:02:06,522
I wanted to hurry
and have a drink with you.

32
00:02:10,985 --> 00:02:11,819
Let's toast.

33
00:02:12,403 --> 00:02:13,655
-Cheers!
-Hold it.

34
00:02:14,405 --> 00:02:16,282
Instead of clinking glasses,

35
00:02:17,492 --> 00:02:19,285
I'd rather bump something else first.

36
00:02:27,377 --> 00:02:29,254
-Man, what the hell?
-What?

37
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:34,259
Holy smokes.

38
00:02:35,051 --> 00:02:37,929
I thought you went home a while ago.

39
00:02:38,012 --> 00:02:40,139
I did, but I came back.

40
00:02:43,309 --> 00:02:44,143
Do you

41
00:02:45,019 --> 00:02:47,897
just go for it like that?

42
00:02:49,357 --> 00:02:52,485
Without setting the mood or anything?

43
00:02:52,568 --> 00:02:56,239
Is it normal to just go for it like that?

44
00:02:57,532 --> 00:02:59,617
You're asking that at your age?

45
00:03:01,452 --> 00:03:02,620
I should get going.

46
00:03:02,704 --> 00:03:04,956
-No, please stay.
-No.

47
00:03:05,039 --> 00:03:07,542
-Tae-ha, I brought some eel.
-Right.

48
00:03:07,625 --> 00:03:09,544
-No, I'm good.
-It's great for you.

49
00:03:09,627 --> 00:03:12,380
No, Tae-ha.
That ginseng liquor is good for you too.

50
00:03:12,463 --> 00:03:14,674
-Please…
-Drink up. I'll get going.

51
00:03:14,757 --> 00:03:15,591
But…

52
00:03:19,053 --> 00:03:20,638
Darn it.

53
00:03:26,311 --> 00:03:27,812
Looks like I

54
00:03:28,646 --> 00:03:29,480
interrupted.

55
00:03:29,564 --> 00:03:30,982
Oh, forget it.

56
00:03:33,901 --> 00:03:34,986
What the…

57
00:03:35,486 --> 00:03:39,574
Why the heck are your cheeks so red?

58
00:03:39,657 --> 00:03:41,242
Did you get beat up?

59
00:03:42,452 --> 00:03:44,579
Come on. You think I'd get beaten up?

60
00:03:44,662 --> 00:03:46,331
I'm asking because you're not.

61
00:03:46,414 --> 00:03:47,790
Tell me.

62
00:03:48,291 --> 00:03:49,917
Why are your cheeks on fire?

63
00:03:55,131 --> 00:03:56,424
Seriously.

64
00:03:56,507 --> 00:04:00,219
You got spooked and almost blew it
over a kiss? And you call yourself a man?

65
00:04:00,303 --> 00:04:02,055
I wasn't spooked.

66
00:04:02,138 --> 00:04:03,848
Don't tell me it was your first.

67
00:04:04,932 --> 00:04:07,310
Don't ask. It's a pride matter.

68
00:04:07,393 --> 00:04:08,936
"Fried"? As in fried chicken?

69
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:11,356
You mean it's "private."

70
00:04:11,981 --> 00:04:13,232
F-R…

71
00:04:14,525 --> 00:04:15,443
You know?

72
00:04:16,069 --> 00:04:20,114
Yikes, I should've made sure
you hit some books too.

73
00:04:20,656 --> 00:04:24,744
Why would you try to use
our story as yours in the first place?

74
00:04:24,827 --> 00:04:28,623
Besides, it wasn't even a toad.
It was a snake.

75
00:04:28,706 --> 00:04:31,834
At the very least,
you need to be able to catch a snake

76
00:04:31,918 --> 00:04:34,879
to make a girl swoon and fall for you.

77
00:04:34,962 --> 00:04:37,256
If you told someone
they fell for you over a toad,

78
00:04:37,340 --> 00:04:40,093
who'd believe that, you foolish toad?

79
00:04:40,676 --> 00:04:44,430
I don't know.
My mind totally blanked for a second.

80
00:04:44,931 --> 00:04:46,057
Oh man.

81
00:04:48,142 --> 00:04:49,560
Unbelievable.

82
00:04:49,644 --> 00:04:52,855
I can't believe I'm seeing
the great Jang Tae-ha so humiliated.

83
00:04:52,939 --> 00:04:53,856
Goodness.

84
00:04:55,066 --> 00:04:58,027
Hey, since we're on the topic,
let me ask you something.

85
00:04:58,111 --> 00:05:00,988
What kind of debt
do you owe Prosecutor Go exactly?

86
00:05:01,072 --> 00:05:05,535
What could she have done to make you
save her from the brink of death?

87
00:05:05,618 --> 00:05:09,705
And why do you go as stiff as a plank
when you're with her?

88
00:05:10,498 --> 00:05:13,501
You've actually met her before.

89
00:05:15,211 --> 00:05:17,213
I've met Ms. Prosecutor before?

90
00:05:21,926 --> 00:05:23,553
Remember me when you make it.

91
00:05:23,636 --> 00:05:26,639
Without me,
you would have missed out on a medal.

92
00:05:27,306 --> 00:05:30,017
When I win Olympic gold,
I'll shout you out in my interview.

93
00:05:31,060 --> 00:05:34,147
It was nice meeting you,
Mr. Future Gold Medalist.

94
00:05:40,111 --> 00:05:41,154
No way.

95
00:05:41,237 --> 00:05:43,698
That feisty high school girl

96
00:05:44,449 --> 00:05:45,450
is Prosecutor Go?

97
00:05:47,368 --> 00:05:48,703
We parted ways like that

98
00:05:50,079 --> 00:05:51,664
but met again eight years ago.

99
00:05:53,166 --> 00:05:55,501
8 YEARS AGO, JAPAN

100
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:36,626
Why are you here?

101
00:06:42,340 --> 00:06:43,966
Who are you?

102
00:06:44,050 --> 00:06:46,219
Come on, this is a VIP room.

103
00:06:46,302 --> 00:06:47,762
Go on. Get out of here.

104
00:06:53,893 --> 00:06:54,810
Kill them!

105
00:06:58,147 --> 00:06:59,440
Charge!

106
00:07:14,455 --> 00:07:15,790
You bastards!

107
00:07:25,466 --> 00:07:26,884
Come here, you bastard!

108
00:07:40,398 --> 00:07:41,482
Hey.

109
00:08:05,214 --> 00:08:07,717
Please don't kill me.

110
00:08:08,551 --> 00:08:11,178
Count up what you've been skimming
and send over our share.

111
00:08:11,804 --> 00:08:13,556
Pull something like that again,

112
00:08:15,057 --> 00:08:16,642
and it won't end at this.

113
00:08:17,768 --> 00:08:19,312
Yes, understood.

114
00:08:40,249 --> 00:08:44,503
Sir, everything's been taken care of,
and it's drizzling.

115
00:08:44,587 --> 00:08:46,297
How about some sake?

116
00:08:46,797 --> 00:08:47,632
I'm good.

117
00:08:48,132 --> 00:08:50,885
Don't mind me.
Go relax and have fun with the boys.

118
00:08:50,968 --> 00:08:54,722
Come on. How could we relax
and have fun without you?

119
00:08:54,805 --> 00:08:56,766
This card should do the trick.

120
00:08:58,809 --> 00:08:59,977
Thank you very much.

121
00:09:00,061 --> 00:09:01,020
Thank you.

122
00:09:01,520 --> 00:09:02,438
We'll see you later.

123
00:09:13,574 --> 00:09:15,201
That's him. Let's go.

124
00:10:15,511 --> 00:10:16,637
Get him!

125
00:10:19,014 --> 00:10:21,684
-Hey, stop right there!
-Stop!

126
00:10:28,399 --> 00:10:29,233
Get him!

127
00:10:45,583 --> 00:10:47,042
Step aside. Move!

128
00:10:50,045 --> 00:10:51,338
The hell do you think I am?

129
00:10:53,382 --> 00:10:54,467
Die!

130
00:10:55,843 --> 00:10:58,679
-What's this?
-What's this?

131
00:11:04,226 --> 00:11:05,186
Hop on, quick!

132
00:11:06,228 --> 00:11:07,062
Hurry!

133
00:11:16,739 --> 00:11:18,407
Get out of the way!

134
00:11:35,382 --> 00:11:36,550
Faster!

135
00:12:40,739 --> 00:12:43,742
-How did you--
-How did I know you were Korean?

136
00:12:44,243 --> 00:12:47,121
I saw you tell your friends
to have fun with your card earlier.

137
00:12:47,913 --> 00:12:52,293
But the people who followed you
looked pretty dangerous.

138
00:12:53,210 --> 00:12:55,838
There are a lot of yakuza here,
so you have to be careful.

139
00:13:05,055 --> 00:13:05,890
Something wrong?

140
00:13:11,228 --> 00:13:12,396
By any chance,

141
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:14,773
have we met before?

142
00:13:24,325 --> 00:13:26,160
2010 NATIONAL JUNIOR BOXING TEAM SELECTION

143
00:13:51,936 --> 00:13:52,895
I guess not.

144
00:14:05,366 --> 00:14:06,659
Yeah, I got away for now.

145
00:14:07,409 --> 00:14:09,411
I'll find my way back.
No need to come here.

146
00:14:09,495 --> 00:14:10,913
You guys move hotels. Now.

147
00:14:25,302 --> 00:14:26,720
What should I do?

148
00:14:26,804 --> 00:14:28,806
I don't have any gas to get back.

149
00:14:30,182 --> 00:14:33,477
I guess I rode a bit too hard earlier.

150
00:14:34,186 --> 00:14:36,063
Then we should call the rental company--

151
00:14:36,146 --> 00:14:39,316
It's the middle of the night,
so they'll be closed.

152
00:14:44,405 --> 00:14:47,116
I guess we have no choice.
There's only one option.

153
00:14:47,616 --> 00:14:49,994
Time will pass, and the sun will rise.

154
00:14:50,494 --> 00:14:51,912
Let's wait until morning.

155
00:14:58,919 --> 00:14:59,878
You're bleeding.

156
00:15:00,963 --> 00:15:03,590
You must've gotten hurt earlier.

157
00:15:08,512 --> 00:15:09,680
That's got to hurt.

158
00:15:21,817 --> 00:15:24,361
All done. It won't get infected now.

159
00:15:25,446 --> 00:15:27,072
You carry Band-Aids with you?

160
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:29,658
The backs of my heels chafe a lot.

161
00:15:31,076 --> 00:15:34,079
And you carry whiskey with you?

162
00:15:35,372 --> 00:15:38,083
I've only seen people carry these
in movies.

163
00:15:38,167 --> 00:15:39,710
Never in real life.

164
00:15:40,294 --> 00:15:41,795
You must really like alcohol.

165
00:15:41,879 --> 00:15:45,883
Or do you often feel like getting drunk?

166
00:15:51,555 --> 00:15:54,016
Hey, wait a minute.
You're putting it away?

167
00:15:54,099 --> 00:15:55,934
It seemed like there was some left.

168
00:16:02,191 --> 00:16:05,861
What else is there to do on a long night?
We might as well drink.

169
00:16:05,944 --> 00:16:06,779
That's strong…

170
00:16:10,741 --> 00:16:11,658
Perfect.

171
00:16:14,995 --> 00:16:16,955
Did you come out here with your friends?

172
00:16:22,044 --> 00:16:23,087
I came alone.

173
00:16:23,170 --> 00:16:27,049
I'd been feeling down
since breaking up with my boyfriend.

174
00:16:28,759 --> 00:16:31,720
It's normal to struggle
to get over your first love, right?

175
00:17:13,971 --> 00:17:16,223
My name is Go Ji-won.

176
00:17:16,306 --> 00:17:19,184
But apparently my real name is Go Eun-sae.

177
00:17:22,479 --> 00:17:23,647
-Go Eun-sae.
-Yeah.

178
00:17:24,857 --> 00:17:28,902
My mom left me at an orphanage
right after she had me.

179
00:17:28,986 --> 00:17:32,614
The head of the orphanage
registered me as Go Ji-won,

180
00:17:33,115 --> 00:17:36,243
but my name was Go Eun-sae
in my mom's maternity notebook.

181
00:17:36,743 --> 00:17:37,828
Pretty name, huh?

182
00:17:40,497 --> 00:17:41,832
That's why

183
00:17:42,624 --> 00:17:45,002
I'm pretty sure my mom loved me.

184
00:17:45,085 --> 00:17:49,131
Who would give such a pretty name
to a baby they don't love?

185
00:17:49,715 --> 00:17:50,591
Don't you think?

186
00:17:53,218 --> 00:17:54,803
What's your name?

187
00:17:58,974 --> 00:18:00,517
Jang Tae-ha.

188
00:18:02,352 --> 00:18:03,687
That's a really solid name.

189
00:18:05,981 --> 00:18:07,191
What do you do for work?

190
00:18:11,403 --> 00:18:14,198
You don't have to tell me
if you don't want to.

191
00:18:14,281 --> 00:18:16,116
As long as you're not a gangster.

192
00:18:21,371 --> 00:18:22,206
You see,

193
00:18:23,290 --> 00:18:26,251
I'm going to become a prosecutor
who catches bad guys.

194
00:18:26,335 --> 00:18:27,794
I'm in law school right now.

195
00:18:33,383 --> 00:18:36,011
This place is so beautiful.

196
00:18:39,473 --> 00:18:42,726
I bet living somewhere like this
would feel like a dream.

197
00:18:49,024 --> 00:18:49,983
Take a picture of me.

198
00:19:07,209 --> 00:19:08,627
Thank you.

199
00:19:11,380 --> 00:19:12,839
I wonder how it'll turn out.

200
00:19:14,466 --> 00:19:16,176
You must like taking pictures.

201
00:19:16,260 --> 00:19:19,012
Yeah, I've been taking pictures
since I was a kid.

202
00:19:24,101 --> 00:19:26,103
Shall we take one together?

203
00:19:28,522 --> 00:19:29,523
It's actually…

204
00:19:33,277 --> 00:19:34,736
my birthday today.

205
00:19:37,281 --> 00:19:38,782
To celebrate.

206
00:19:38,865 --> 00:19:40,075
Well?

207
00:19:50,544 --> 00:19:52,629
What are you doing? Get over here.

208
00:20:28,957 --> 00:20:30,876
Back in elementary school,

209
00:20:30,959 --> 00:20:33,545
my eraser rolled over
to my desk mate's side,

210
00:20:33,628 --> 00:20:34,671
and all of a sudden,

211
00:20:34,755 --> 00:20:37,007
they stabbed me in the butt
with their pencil.

212
00:20:37,090 --> 00:20:38,383
Isn't that ridiculous?

213
00:20:38,467 --> 00:20:43,305
I'd always had two moles on my butt
just below where they stabbed me.

214
00:20:43,388 --> 00:20:47,934
The lead stabbed me in the perfect spot
to make a triangle with the two moles.

215
00:20:48,018 --> 00:20:50,812
So the mole on top is a different color.

216
00:20:53,273 --> 00:20:55,817
It's like a pyramid. So stupid.

217
00:23:17,167 --> 00:23:18,293
The sun's up.

218
00:23:34,392 --> 00:23:36,228
Happy birthday.

219
00:24:07,717 --> 00:24:08,635
All set.

220
00:24:12,264 --> 00:24:15,976
There's no need to thank me,
since I also had fun thanks to you.

221
00:24:23,692 --> 00:24:25,402
When we go back to Korea…

222
00:24:27,612 --> 00:24:29,072
can we keep in touch?

223
00:24:38,957 --> 00:24:40,125
If not, never mind.

224
00:24:48,466 --> 00:24:49,342
If we meet again…

225
00:24:52,012 --> 00:24:53,680
I'll make sure to pay back the debt.

226
00:25:00,687 --> 00:25:02,647
You better keep that promise.

227
00:25:04,149 --> 00:25:05,191
I'll be off, then.

228
00:25:46,983 --> 00:25:48,568
Damn.

229
00:25:49,235 --> 00:25:50,820
That's some fateful encounter.

230
00:25:52,072 --> 00:25:54,532
You know, all this time,

231
00:25:54,616 --> 00:25:57,994
I thought what we had here
was a film noir.

232
00:25:58,495 --> 00:25:59,704
But, man!

233
00:26:00,455 --> 00:26:02,916
Turns out it was a romance.

234
00:26:02,999 --> 00:26:04,459
It's not like that.

235
00:26:04,542 --> 00:26:08,630
I promised I would repay the debt,
and she said I'd better keep that promise.

236
00:26:10,006 --> 00:26:12,926
Besides, promises are meant to be kept.

237
00:26:13,885 --> 00:26:16,471
We call that the stuff of romance.

238
00:26:18,640 --> 00:26:19,849
Man.

239
00:26:20,350 --> 00:26:23,812
I thought you were a guy
who didn't know a thing about women.

240
00:26:23,895 --> 00:26:25,522
I'm proud of you, Jang Tae-ha.

241
00:26:25,605 --> 00:26:30,068
You have feelings for someone
buried deep in your heart.

242
00:26:31,778 --> 00:26:34,114
She didn't seem to dislike me before,

243
00:26:34,197 --> 00:26:37,534
so I don't get
why she's nitpicking everything

244
00:26:38,034 --> 00:26:39,411
and is suspicious of me now.

245
00:26:40,912 --> 00:26:43,957
Do you think it's because of my hairstyle?

246
00:26:44,040 --> 00:26:46,209
Maybe you weren't prepared enough.

247
00:26:47,127 --> 00:26:50,296
You should've bought some clothes
from a department store in Seoul.

248
00:26:50,380 --> 00:26:52,882
She's a young woman,
and you filled her closet

249
00:26:52,966 --> 00:26:55,218
with cheap clothes from the street market.

250
00:26:55,301 --> 00:26:58,096
Hey, your wife bought
all of those, remember?

251
00:26:59,431 --> 00:27:01,808
Jeong-hwa's taste is a bit old-school.

252
00:27:01,891 --> 00:27:05,812
And, to top it off, you're the one
who recommended that flowery blanket.

253
00:27:05,895 --> 00:27:08,231
Hey, don't women like flowers?

254
00:27:11,025 --> 00:27:13,528
That's what I thought too.

255
00:27:16,114 --> 00:27:18,867
Whatever. Look.

256
00:27:19,701 --> 00:27:20,952
There's only one way.

257
00:27:22,412 --> 00:27:24,873
You can't get flustered.

258
00:27:26,124 --> 00:27:28,209
Even if something like this happens again,

259
00:27:28,293 --> 00:27:31,129
you absolutely cannot get spooked.

260
00:27:32,005 --> 00:27:33,882
When you've lived together for two years,

261
00:27:33,965 --> 00:27:38,011
you're bound to bump lips all the time.

262
00:27:38,970 --> 00:27:40,889
Some days, it gets pretty intense.

263
00:27:42,223 --> 00:27:43,183
And some days,

264
00:27:43,850 --> 00:27:45,685
it won't end at just lips.

265
00:27:49,773 --> 00:27:52,025
The heck? What are you, a traffic light?

266
00:27:52,108 --> 00:27:53,902
Why do you keep turning red?

267
00:27:53,985 --> 00:27:54,819
Me?

268
00:27:56,529 --> 00:27:58,198
Look at you.

269
00:28:05,288 --> 00:28:08,166
Judging by the kiss,
I'm certain he's not my boyfriend.

270
00:28:09,626 --> 00:28:11,169
Then why did he bring me here?

271
00:28:13,463 --> 00:28:15,548
Maybe he was my stalker who…

272
00:28:16,549 --> 00:28:18,885
He's way too unfriendly for that.

273
00:28:19,969 --> 00:28:21,971
Or was I kidnapped?

274
00:28:23,097 --> 00:28:24,098
Am I filthy rich?

275
00:28:26,392 --> 00:28:29,020
Seriously, what is all this?

276
00:28:29,103 --> 00:28:31,856
I'm absolutely clueless.

277
00:28:45,328 --> 00:28:46,329
Good job.

278
00:29:02,679 --> 00:29:03,847
I've got a headache.

279
00:30:17,045 --> 00:30:17,879
What is it?

280
00:30:19,964 --> 00:30:20,965
Let's have breakfast.

281
00:30:21,633 --> 00:30:22,842
I'm not hungry.

282
00:30:22,926 --> 00:30:25,428
You didn't even touch the sushi
I brought last night.

283
00:30:27,722 --> 00:30:30,433
How could I eat it
when I don't know what's in it?

284
00:30:30,516 --> 00:30:32,560
Since it's from my non-boyfriend.

285
00:30:35,939 --> 00:30:37,523
If you can't trust me,

286
00:30:38,399 --> 00:30:40,193
at least buy yourself something to eat.

287
00:30:40,735 --> 00:30:41,986
You shouldn't starve.

288
00:30:56,542 --> 00:31:00,213
Everything must feel unfamiliar,
so I wanted to stay with you,

289
00:31:00,296 --> 00:31:02,382
but I have somewhere to be today.

290
00:31:02,966 --> 00:31:04,133
It's something important.

291
00:31:04,676 --> 00:31:05,510
I'm sorry.

292
00:31:05,593 --> 00:31:07,470
It's totally fine.

293
00:31:07,971 --> 00:31:09,347
I couldn't care less.

294
00:31:09,430 --> 00:31:11,641
Still, being alone might be a bit weird,

295
00:31:12,392 --> 00:31:13,476
so I invited someone.

296
00:31:16,562 --> 00:31:19,482
It's been a while, Ms. Eun-sae.

297
00:31:19,565 --> 00:31:21,818
We've met before too?

298
00:31:23,444 --> 00:31:24,904
Well, of course.

299
00:31:25,488 --> 00:31:27,907
I was your closest friend in the village.

300
00:31:28,491 --> 00:31:29,492
Sorry?

301
00:31:30,243 --> 00:31:32,996
Well, then. Please take good care of her.

302
00:31:33,079 --> 00:31:35,039
Sure. Don't worry and go.

303
00:31:35,123 --> 00:31:35,957
Go on.

304
00:31:40,795 --> 00:31:41,671
I won't be late.

305
00:31:49,554 --> 00:31:51,764
I guess he doesn't wear sweats
all the time.

306
00:31:51,848 --> 00:31:53,933
Quite dashing, isn't he?

307
00:31:54,475 --> 00:31:57,478
Men look best in suits.

308
00:31:59,188 --> 00:32:03,317
My husband in a suit would knock
Park Bo-gum right out of the park.

309
00:32:03,818 --> 00:32:05,862
There's such a man in this village?

310
00:32:16,789 --> 00:32:17,665
You look different.

311
00:32:21,294 --> 00:32:23,129
So you cleared out your place in Seoul.

312
00:32:25,590 --> 00:32:26,424
Yes, sir.

313
00:32:26,966 --> 00:32:28,551
Thank you for everything.

314
00:32:29,886 --> 00:32:31,888
I know you like wine,
so I got this for you.

315
00:32:33,264 --> 00:32:34,140
Please accept it.

316
00:32:36,142 --> 00:32:38,895
A parting gift, is it?

317
00:32:38,978 --> 00:32:43,274
It's nothing compared to how
you've taken care of me over the years.

318
00:32:43,357 --> 00:32:46,986
A bottle of wine worth 100 million won
is nothing?

319
00:32:50,073 --> 00:32:51,282
Tell me, is this real?

320
00:32:52,408 --> 00:32:53,242
Sorry?

321
00:32:54,202 --> 00:32:57,371
Romanée-Conti is a wine
that has a lot of counterfeits.

322
00:32:58,706 --> 00:33:00,875
I paid full price
at a wine auction in Spain.

323
00:33:01,751 --> 00:33:02,835
It's authentic.

324
00:33:03,419 --> 00:33:06,923
Turns out, money isn't a reliable way
to tell what's real from what's fake.

325
00:33:07,632 --> 00:33:09,217
Sometimes, you pay the full price

326
00:33:09,967 --> 00:33:11,719
and still get fooled.

327
00:33:15,515 --> 00:33:18,017
I would never give you anything fake, sir.

328
00:33:18,601 --> 00:33:19,727
Of course not.

329
00:33:19,811 --> 00:33:21,062
Jang Tae-ha.

330
00:33:22,522 --> 00:33:24,482
You've never once disappointed me.

331
00:33:25,817 --> 00:33:27,193
I don't know about the others,

332
00:33:27,902 --> 00:33:28,945
but I trust you.

333
00:33:34,158 --> 00:33:35,284
So what's the plan?

334
00:33:36,410 --> 00:33:37,829
I'll put my gloves back on.

335
00:33:46,796 --> 00:33:47,630
Boxing?

336
00:33:49,298 --> 00:33:50,216
Yes, sir.

337
00:33:50,299 --> 00:33:51,467
So…

338
00:33:56,514 --> 00:33:58,099
I'm returning this to you.

339
00:34:03,437 --> 00:34:05,481
It's a gift for taking off your gloves.

340
00:34:06,357 --> 00:34:09,610
From now on, get in fights
that reek of blood, not sweat.

341
00:34:19,871 --> 00:34:22,540
GUJIN TAFFY VILLAGE

342
00:34:22,623 --> 00:34:25,293
That place has great braised monkfish.

343
00:34:27,044 --> 00:34:31,215
And this place
does an amazing pollack stew.

344
00:34:31,799 --> 00:34:33,217
What would you like?

345
00:34:34,218 --> 00:34:37,555
You claim we were close,
but you don't know a thing about me.

346
00:34:37,638 --> 00:34:39,640
I don't like spicy foods.

347
00:34:40,224 --> 00:34:42,977
I didn't eat anything smothered in sauce
at the hospital.

348
00:34:44,395 --> 00:34:45,605
Is that so?

349
00:34:45,688 --> 00:34:49,150
So you can drop the act now.
I don't believe you.

350
00:34:50,318 --> 00:34:53,905
I'm going to figure out
why Mr. Jang Tae-ha is lying

351
00:34:53,988 --> 00:34:55,281
just to keep me here.

352
00:34:55,364 --> 00:34:56,490
Okay.

353
00:34:56,574 --> 00:34:57,992
Then why don't we eat

354
00:34:58,075 --> 00:35:02,622
the tofu poke you used to love
and figure it out?

355
00:35:04,081 --> 00:35:05,458
Have you tried tofu poke?

356
00:35:05,541 --> 00:35:07,460
It's delicious.

357
00:35:07,543 --> 00:35:09,670
You don't eat rice
because you're on a diet.

358
00:35:09,754 --> 00:35:13,007
If you want to slim down, it's all about
going hard on your meal plan.

359
00:35:14,091 --> 00:35:15,134
I know all about you.

360
00:35:16,802 --> 00:35:20,389
If you don't believe me,
figure things out on your own.

361
00:35:21,307 --> 00:35:22,808
Or don't.

362
00:35:22,892 --> 00:35:24,518
Boy, the weather's nice.

363
00:35:24,602 --> 00:35:26,812
Maybe I'll stop by the gym?

364
00:35:26,896 --> 00:35:29,565
Come here and have some tofu salad.

365
00:35:29,649 --> 00:35:31,317
It's called poke.

366
00:35:31,400 --> 00:35:33,402
I only know about it because of Eun-sae.

367
00:35:33,486 --> 00:35:37,740
It just looks like a bunch of raw veggies,
but that's what the kids call it.

368
00:35:37,823 --> 00:35:40,660
It's all just for show.

369
00:35:40,743 --> 00:35:41,577
Oh my.

370
00:35:42,745 --> 00:35:45,581
On your face, even a grain of rice

371
00:35:46,082 --> 00:35:48,042
looks like a diamond, honey.

372
00:35:51,921 --> 00:35:53,005
That's right.

373
00:35:53,089 --> 00:35:54,006
Park Bo-gum.

374
00:35:55,341 --> 00:35:57,260
What do you think? Isn't he handsome?

375
00:35:58,469 --> 00:36:03,057
When he's all dressed up, he really does
knock Park Bo-gum out of the park.

376
00:36:03,641 --> 00:36:06,185
If Park Bo-gum heard that,
he'd knock him out all right.

377
00:36:07,186 --> 00:36:09,855
So you're saying
I used to come here often?

378
00:36:10,564 --> 00:36:11,816
-Yeah.
-Of course.

379
00:36:12,400 --> 00:36:16,279
We used to eat together like this,
right here, all the time.

380
00:36:18,614 --> 00:36:19,699
You don't believe me?

381
00:36:20,199 --> 00:36:22,034
She's very suspicious.

382
00:36:22,118 --> 00:36:24,620
Let's see. What could we…

383
00:36:25,329 --> 00:36:26,330
Right.

384
00:36:26,414 --> 00:36:27,748
These coupons here.

385
00:36:27,832 --> 00:36:32,336
We collected so many
because you often ate with us.

386
00:36:32,420 --> 00:36:33,796
And what else?

387
00:36:33,879 --> 00:36:35,631
Darn, my eyes are so blurry.

388
00:36:35,715 --> 00:36:38,426
Then what's my go-to noodle order?
Three, two, one.

389
00:36:38,509 --> 00:36:40,094
-Spicy!
-Black bean… spicy.

390
00:36:43,014 --> 00:36:44,015
"Black bean spicy"?

391
00:36:47,393 --> 00:36:50,771
Do you honestly expect me
to believe any of this?

392
00:36:52,940 --> 00:36:55,693
Whatever. This neighborhood
has a psychiatrist, right?

393
00:36:56,610 --> 00:36:57,445
Why do you ask?

394
00:36:57,528 --> 00:37:00,197
I can't get a background check
with these fingers,

395
00:37:00,281 --> 00:37:02,199
so even the police can't help me.

396
00:37:02,783 --> 00:37:05,995
I figured I'd get my head checked
since I need my memory back fast.

397
00:37:12,501 --> 00:37:13,336
What is it?

398
00:37:14,045 --> 00:37:17,923
Is there any reason I can't get treatment
and get my memory back?

399
00:37:18,007 --> 00:37:20,384
Not at all.
You should get your memory back.

400
00:37:21,385 --> 00:37:22,595
-Yeah.
-What are you doing?

401
00:37:22,678 --> 00:37:24,055
Take her there in Bluey.

402
00:37:24,138 --> 00:37:25,931
Yes, of course.

403
00:37:26,015 --> 00:37:28,476
Let's go after we eat. Let's eat first.

404
00:37:28,559 --> 00:37:30,269
GANGJU CITY HALL

405
00:37:30,353 --> 00:37:31,812
Isn't it a bit odd?

406
00:37:32,396 --> 00:37:35,691
It's been over three weeks,
and not a single word from Prosecutor Go.

407
00:37:35,775 --> 00:37:37,109
Why are you so worried?

408
00:37:39,362 --> 00:37:42,615
You'd think you two dated for real.

409
00:37:43,115 --> 00:37:44,325
Have you grown attached?

410
00:37:44,408 --> 00:37:46,702
I went undercover
to derail the investigation.

411
00:37:46,786 --> 00:37:49,163
-I didn't expect this to happen.
-Exactly.

412
00:37:49,663 --> 00:37:52,666
If you'd kept her at the party,
we wouldn't be in this mess.

413
00:37:53,459 --> 00:37:54,710
Because of your mistake,

414
00:37:54,794 --> 00:37:57,129
I may have to concede a move
to Baek Sang-gil.

415
00:37:57,213 --> 00:37:59,340
Do you know how serious this is?

416
00:38:00,299 --> 00:38:03,052
Don't get all dramatic,
pretending you have morals.

417
00:38:03,135 --> 00:38:04,762
If you're a mole, act like one.

418
00:38:05,679 --> 00:38:07,681
Just do as you're told.

419
00:38:12,895 --> 00:38:16,315
Go Ji-won, just what were you thinking,
disappearing like that?

420
00:38:16,816 --> 00:38:19,860
Since they took your watch,
you probably couldn't do…

421
00:38:19,944 --> 00:38:21,612
Is this your trusty friend?

422
00:38:22,613 --> 00:38:23,447
Yeah.

423
00:38:26,534 --> 00:38:29,203
It better do a good job and not slack off.

424
00:38:30,579 --> 00:38:31,705
Don't worry.

425
00:38:31,789 --> 00:38:32,957
I have backup.

426
00:38:33,040 --> 00:38:34,166
That's right.

427
00:38:34,250 --> 00:38:36,293
The watch wasn't all.

428
00:38:38,504 --> 00:38:41,340
-This van is called Bluey?
-Yes.

429
00:38:42,216 --> 00:38:45,010
We named it because of its bluish color

430
00:38:45,094 --> 00:38:47,054
back when we were dating.

431
00:38:48,556 --> 00:38:51,392
Then it must be quite old.

432
00:38:52,101 --> 00:38:55,521
Vehicles may look different
on the outside,

433
00:38:55,604 --> 00:38:58,065
but the view from the inside
is always the same.

434
00:38:58,149 --> 00:39:00,401
What does it matter
if it looks fancy to others?

435
00:39:00,484 --> 00:39:03,362
What matters most is if it feels familiar
and comfortable to me.

436
00:39:13,080 --> 00:39:14,582
This…

437
00:39:17,835 --> 00:39:18,669
My goodness!

438
00:39:19,253 --> 00:39:21,297
This has never happened to our dear Bluey!

439
00:39:21,380 --> 00:39:24,216
Dear Bluey, are you okay?
Of course you're not!

440
00:39:24,300 --> 00:39:28,137
Familiar and comfortable is good and all,
but a vehicle has to be able to run.

441
00:39:28,220 --> 00:39:30,473
-What should we do?
-Just call the insurance.

442
00:39:30,556 --> 00:39:34,935
I'll call the insurance company,
and you head to the clinic, okay?

443
00:39:35,686 --> 00:39:39,398
By "that way," which way did she mean?
She could have given me proper directions.

444
00:39:39,482 --> 00:39:41,650
Is Bluey her baby or something?

445
00:39:46,155 --> 00:39:47,406
Oh no!

446
00:39:48,866 --> 00:39:50,034
Thank you.

447
00:39:50,117 --> 00:39:51,911
I thought I saw one over here.

448
00:39:51,994 --> 00:39:53,996
Where did it… Excuse me.

449
00:40:02,254 --> 00:40:03,088
Yes?

450
00:40:03,672 --> 00:40:06,258
Hello. If you don't mind,

451
00:40:06,342 --> 00:40:08,886
could you walk me
to that building over there?

452
00:40:10,137 --> 00:40:12,181
AN MENTAL HEALTH CLINIC

453
00:40:12,932 --> 00:40:13,766
Sorry?

454
00:40:13,849 --> 00:40:16,143
It's a waste to buy an umbrella
for a short walk.

455
00:40:18,270 --> 00:40:20,356
I'm also headed there, but I bought one.

456
00:40:20,439 --> 00:40:23,484
Oh, really? That's great.
If you're going that way, I'll join you.

457
00:40:24,777 --> 00:40:27,404
You don't need to worry about
tilting it my way.

458
00:40:30,950 --> 00:40:31,992
All right, then.

459
00:40:32,076 --> 00:40:33,911
-Excuse me.
-What the heck?

460
00:40:34,495 --> 00:40:36,539
-Why are you…
-Could you raise it a little?

461
00:40:36,622 --> 00:40:38,624
-Seriously, who even are you?
-I just…

462
00:40:44,213 --> 00:40:45,965
Would you like me to hold it?

463
00:40:46,048 --> 00:40:48,008
No, I'm good.

464
00:40:49,426 --> 00:40:50,427
I'm uncomfortable.

465
00:41:02,314 --> 00:41:03,482
Watch out!

466
00:41:14,243 --> 00:41:15,077
Your…

467
00:41:16,078 --> 00:41:16,912
Your hair…

468
00:41:25,254 --> 00:41:26,213
Take this…

469
00:41:30,342 --> 00:41:32,177
I'm sorry.

470
00:41:32,261 --> 00:41:34,763
I'm not very athletic.

471
00:41:34,847 --> 00:41:38,100
I was trying to turn us 180 degrees,
but I turned us the full 360.

472
00:41:43,772 --> 00:41:46,233
Not athletic, my ass.

473
00:41:46,942 --> 00:41:48,944
What a real piece of work.

474
00:41:49,028 --> 00:41:50,529
Doors opening.

475
00:41:52,281 --> 00:41:53,115
After you.

476
00:41:54,992 --> 00:41:56,493
I caught some of the splash too.

477
00:41:56,994 --> 00:41:58,579
Sure. Please wait a moment.

478
00:42:01,665 --> 00:42:03,417
-Hello, I…
-It's pouring outside.

479
00:42:03,500 --> 00:42:04,627
-Hello, Dr. An.
-Hi.

480
00:42:07,004 --> 00:42:07,838
Doctor?

481
00:42:11,133 --> 00:42:12,760
Shocker, right?

482
00:42:13,719 --> 00:42:14,595
Well,

483
00:42:15,804 --> 00:42:16,764
this is my clinic.

484
00:42:18,265 --> 00:42:19,850
We have towels, don't we?

485
00:42:19,933 --> 00:42:23,145
Yes, please, Hyang-seon.
The rain got her good.

486
00:42:23,228 --> 00:42:24,396
Oh my God.

487
00:42:30,361 --> 00:42:32,154
DIRECTOR AN GI-JUN

488
00:42:36,200 --> 00:42:37,326
So, you're saying,

489
00:42:37,409 --> 00:42:41,622
even though we can't treat you
because you're technically unidentified,

490
00:42:41,705 --> 00:42:43,624
I should help you get your memory back?

491
00:42:43,707 --> 00:42:46,251
Since I was a bit out of line earlier?

492
00:42:50,047 --> 00:42:52,466
-I'll pay for dry cleaning and umbrella.
-Seriously?

493
00:42:52,549 --> 00:42:55,928
You can continue your treatment
at the hospital you first woke up in.

494
00:42:56,011 --> 00:43:00,015
It's a small country hospital.
They can't give me professional treatment.

495
00:43:00,099 --> 00:43:03,394
I understand your situation,
but we have our own rules and procedures.

496
00:43:03,477 --> 00:43:07,356
Don't rules and procedures come second
to saving people with medicine?

497
00:43:07,439 --> 00:43:11,026
If it was an emergency,
of course I'd do that, but--

498
00:43:11,110 --> 00:43:12,444
This is an emergency!

499
00:43:12,528 --> 00:43:16,657
The man who claims to be my boyfriend
might not be my boyfriend!

500
00:43:16,740 --> 00:43:18,200
Then what would it be?

501
00:43:18,283 --> 00:43:20,452
It's a crime.

502
00:43:20,536 --> 00:43:22,079
Right now, Doctor,

503
00:43:22,579 --> 00:43:26,250
you could be standing by
and letting a crime happen.

504
00:43:26,875 --> 00:43:28,627
-What, me?
-Yes.

505
00:43:28,711 --> 00:43:29,712
But I'm…

506
00:43:30,295 --> 00:43:34,091
Couldn't he really be your boyfriend?

507
00:43:34,591 --> 00:43:37,136
I'm telling you, that's impossible.

508
00:43:37,636 --> 00:43:40,180
First of all, it makes no sense

509
00:43:40,264 --> 00:43:43,809
that I'm in this backwater taffy village
making taffy.

510
00:43:43,892 --> 00:43:46,145
Taffy village? I used to live there.

511
00:43:46,228 --> 00:43:47,062
What?

512
00:43:47,146 --> 00:43:49,523
I know every taffy shop.
Whose shop do you mean?

513
00:43:50,733 --> 00:43:52,276
It's Jang Tae-ha's grandmother's.

514
00:43:54,445 --> 00:43:55,279
Jang Tae-ha?

515
00:43:55,863 --> 00:43:59,366
The guy who claims to be your boyfriend
is Jang Tae-ha?

516
00:43:59,950 --> 00:44:00,784
Yes.

517
00:44:01,827 --> 00:44:02,661
Do you know him?

518
00:44:03,996 --> 00:44:06,582
Well… I see.

519
00:44:11,086 --> 00:44:12,629
DETECTIVE AGENCY

520
00:44:14,047 --> 00:44:14,882
Yes?

521
00:44:14,965 --> 00:44:16,967
Firstly, no hospitals in the capital area

522
00:44:17,050 --> 00:44:18,510
had a patient named Go Ji-won.

523
00:44:19,094 --> 00:44:20,471
Is that so?

524
00:44:20,554 --> 00:44:23,640
But there was a hospital
that had an unidentified patient come in.

525
00:44:23,724 --> 00:44:26,059
A female who looked to be
in her late twenties

526
00:44:26,143 --> 00:44:27,269
to early thirties.

527
00:44:27,352 --> 00:44:28,604
Where is that?

528
00:44:38,197 --> 00:44:41,074
According to our regulations,
we can't just treat you right now.

529
00:44:41,158 --> 00:44:42,743
Come back with Mr. Jang Tae-ha.

530
00:44:42,826 --> 00:44:46,872
We need at least one person who can vouch
for your identity, Ms. Go Eun-sae.

531
00:44:46,955 --> 00:44:49,333
Everyone in this place
is obsessed with Jang Tae-ha.

532
00:44:52,127 --> 00:44:52,961
-Hello.
-Hello.

533
00:44:53,837 --> 00:44:57,591
By any chance, the unidentified patient
who left yesterday morning…

534
00:44:57,674 --> 00:44:58,592
Is this her?

535
00:45:00,385 --> 00:45:01,595
I'm not sure.

536
00:45:01,678 --> 00:45:05,808
She has makeup on,
so I can't tell if it's the same person.

537
00:45:07,559 --> 00:45:09,061
It is the same person.

538
00:45:10,771 --> 00:45:14,358
-Sorry?
-It's the young lady who was in our room.

539
00:45:15,359 --> 00:45:16,193
Are you sure?

540
00:45:16,276 --> 00:45:17,861
Damn right I am.

541
00:45:17,945 --> 00:45:21,782
Her groom-to-be took her home yesterday.

542
00:45:21,865 --> 00:45:22,825
Her groom-to-be?

543
00:45:23,408 --> 00:45:26,829
Ma'am, do you remember
what he looked like?

544
00:45:27,412 --> 00:45:30,332
He was handsome like an actor.

545
00:45:31,291 --> 00:45:33,502
-Hong's…
-Hong's?

546
00:45:34,086 --> 00:45:36,547
Boxing Gym.

547
00:45:36,630 --> 00:45:38,507
That's what it said on the van.

548
00:45:39,091 --> 00:45:40,843
Hong's Boxing Gym?

549
00:45:40,926 --> 00:45:41,760
Yes.

550
00:45:47,975 --> 00:45:50,561
Those ladies are milling around
like gangsters again.

551
00:45:52,187 --> 00:45:55,065
They're no gangsters
but the S.E.S of Taffy Village.

552
00:45:55,148 --> 00:45:56,275
S.E.S?

553
00:45:56,358 --> 00:45:58,360
They might look tough,

554
00:45:58,443 --> 00:46:01,196
but they're actually lovely like fairies.

555
00:46:02,656 --> 00:46:04,992
Do they have different TVs
in Taffy Village?

556
00:46:14,084 --> 00:46:15,419
Ladies!

557
00:46:15,502 --> 00:46:16,378
-Hey!
-Goodness!

558
00:46:17,421 --> 00:46:18,589
I think she's parking.

559
00:46:18,672 --> 00:46:20,007
Who's that with her?

560
00:46:21,133 --> 00:46:22,634
It's that Gen Z kid.

561
00:46:22,718 --> 00:46:24,011
MZ…

562
00:46:29,725 --> 00:46:31,643
"Accurate spiritual readings"?

563
00:46:31,727 --> 00:46:32,561
Yes.

564
00:46:33,061 --> 00:46:35,856
Maeng-suk over there is a fortune teller.

565
00:46:37,024 --> 00:46:38,775
Is she now?

566
00:46:53,040 --> 00:46:53,874
Nothing.

567
00:46:54,458 --> 00:46:55,584
Sorry?

568
00:46:56,168 --> 00:46:58,253
Your face has…

569
00:46:58,337 --> 00:46:59,171
My face?

570
00:46:59,254 --> 00:47:00,422
…no writing.

571
00:47:01,423 --> 00:47:03,342
-There's no writing?
-Yeah.

572
00:47:03,425 --> 00:47:06,303
It means she can't have been
a judge or a prosecutor.

573
00:47:06,386 --> 00:47:08,555
Yeah, I can tell that much too.

574
00:47:08,639 --> 00:47:10,515
-Yeah.
-Then what was I?

575
00:47:10,599 --> 00:47:12,601
Then what could you have been?

576
00:47:12,684 --> 00:47:15,062
What could you have been? Let's see.

577
00:47:18,440 --> 00:47:22,110
Your name is Go Eun-sae.
Not much luck with parents or siblings.

578
00:47:22,694 --> 00:47:25,697
You were born in the fall,
in the Year of the Black Rooster,

579
00:47:25,781 --> 00:47:27,532
which means you have the Hwagae sign.

580
00:47:27,616 --> 00:47:32,162
That means you've got a knack
for the arts, pleasure, and even gambling.

581
00:47:32,245 --> 00:47:34,289
But if someone helps keep you in check,

582
00:47:34,373 --> 00:47:36,833
you can get through relatively unscathed.

583
00:47:36,917 --> 00:47:37,876
And that someone

584
00:47:38,418 --> 00:47:40,253
is Tae-ha, or so my spirit tells me.

585
00:47:40,337 --> 00:47:41,254
Yes.

586
00:47:41,338 --> 00:47:44,424
My, Maeng-suk. You're on a roll.

587
00:47:47,052 --> 00:47:48,553
I see.

588
00:47:51,098 --> 00:47:53,767
You know, while I was in the hospital…

589
00:47:53,850 --> 00:47:54,685
Yes?

590
00:47:54,768 --> 00:47:56,269
I did all kinds of experiments

591
00:47:56,353 --> 00:47:58,814
to try and find out what I was good at.

592
00:47:58,897 --> 00:48:03,902
-You did?
-But I was absolutely awful at drawing.

593
00:48:04,403 --> 00:48:07,114
And seeing how I couldn't figure out
the rules of Go-Stop

594
00:48:07,197 --> 00:48:08,865
even after watching the ladies play,

595
00:48:08,949 --> 00:48:11,159
I don't think I have a knack for gambling.

596
00:48:11,243 --> 00:48:13,078
So her reading's wrong?

597
00:48:14,287 --> 00:48:16,957
Be honest. You're not actually
spiritually gifted, are you?

598
00:48:18,166 --> 00:48:20,627
-What?
-You know everyone in the village.

599
00:48:20,711 --> 00:48:24,256
You probably know all about them,
down to the cutlery in their homes,

600
00:48:24,339 --> 00:48:25,632
so your readings were right.

601
00:48:25,716 --> 00:48:29,261
But you can't guess anything right
about an outsider like me.

602
00:48:30,512 --> 00:48:32,305
-It's pretty much a scam.
-What?

603
00:48:32,389 --> 00:48:34,558
-Scam…
-Scam?

604
00:48:36,560 --> 00:48:38,520
Enough. Get out.

605
00:48:38,603 --> 00:48:39,521
Out at once!

606
00:48:39,604 --> 00:48:42,774
My spirit is livid and refuses to tell you
anything else, so get out.

607
00:48:43,400 --> 00:48:46,987
What kind of spirit gets upset so easily
and refuses to say anything?

608
00:48:47,070 --> 00:48:50,115
Shouldn't spirits be more generous
than humans?

609
00:48:50,198 --> 00:48:52,159
What are you yapping about right now?

610
00:48:52,242 --> 00:48:53,285
You heard me.

611
00:48:57,205 --> 00:49:00,000
I can't give you this. Goodbye.

612
00:49:01,001 --> 00:49:02,753
I can't let you do that.

613
00:49:03,587 --> 00:49:05,047
I can't let you do that either.

614
00:49:07,924 --> 00:49:08,759
Why, you…

615
00:49:09,468 --> 00:49:11,762
What the hell do you think you're doing?

616
00:49:14,765 --> 00:49:16,475
What are you doing?

617
00:49:16,558 --> 00:49:17,517
I just…

618
00:49:17,601 --> 00:49:19,811
I won't let go until you pay me
for the reading.

619
00:49:19,895 --> 00:49:23,315
You didn't get anything right.
Why should I pay you?

620
00:49:23,398 --> 00:49:25,692
-Let go.
-You said you don't remember anything.

621
00:49:25,776 --> 00:49:28,028
So how would you know
if I'm right or wrong?

622
00:49:28,111 --> 00:49:29,196
-How?
-That hurts!

623
00:49:29,279 --> 00:49:31,364
-Hey, both of you. Let's talk it out.
-Let go!

624
00:49:31,448 --> 00:49:33,492
I can't let go until you pay me.

625
00:49:33,575 --> 00:49:35,285
Let go!

626
00:49:44,211 --> 00:49:45,504
-Who did that?
-I don't know.

627
00:49:45,587 --> 00:49:48,423
-Oh, revered spirit!
-Oh dear.

628
00:49:50,425 --> 00:49:52,385
The person who broke my revered spirit

629
00:49:52,886 --> 00:49:54,763
should pay for it, of course!

630
00:49:54,846 --> 00:49:56,765
Who else should pay for it?

631
00:49:56,848 --> 00:49:59,643
How do we know
whether I broke it or you did?

632
00:49:59,726 --> 00:50:01,353
-What did you say?
-What?

633
00:50:01,853 --> 00:50:04,439
The reason this happened
in the first place

634
00:50:04,523 --> 00:50:06,775
is because you refused to pay
for your reading.

635
00:50:06,858 --> 00:50:07,692
Exactly.

636
00:50:07,776 --> 00:50:10,320
If you hadn't tried to scam me
in the first place,

637
00:50:10,403 --> 00:50:11,696
I would have paid you.

638
00:50:11,780 --> 00:50:13,490
-Scam?
-Scam?

639
00:50:14,241 --> 00:50:15,534
-Easy.
-Ms. Eun-sae.

640
00:50:15,617 --> 00:50:16,701
-Ms. Eun-sae.
-Okay.

641
00:50:16,785 --> 00:50:20,372
Okay. Let's say that, in your opinion,
none of the readings were correct.

642
00:50:21,206 --> 00:50:24,167
Even so, Maeng-suk is your elder.

643
00:50:24,251 --> 00:50:28,004
It's not right for you
to talk to her like that. Don't you agree?

644
00:50:29,631 --> 00:50:30,757
-That's right.
-Ma'am.

645
00:50:31,591 --> 00:50:33,135
What's age got to do with it?

646
00:50:33,718 --> 00:50:36,888
If you're older, can't you be called out
for doing something wrong?

647
00:50:37,472 --> 00:50:39,266
Then I guess this grandma here

648
00:50:39,349 --> 00:50:42,686
is free to scam all of you ladies,
since she's the oldest.

649
00:50:43,186 --> 00:50:44,312
What do you mean?

650
00:50:44,396 --> 00:50:46,565
I'm only 17.

651
00:50:47,357 --> 00:50:51,528
Where did you learn
to twist people's words like that?

652
00:50:52,237 --> 00:50:53,071
I'm sorry.

653
00:50:54,322 --> 00:50:55,198
Tae-ha!

654
00:50:55,282 --> 00:50:57,075
Tae-ha, look at how she's acting.

655
00:50:57,159 --> 00:50:58,451
-Tae-ha.
-How could she…

656
00:51:00,120 --> 00:51:01,872
I'll pay for the damage.

657
00:51:02,873 --> 00:51:04,708
Tell me the amount with the reading fee.

658
00:51:06,960 --> 00:51:07,878
Why would you…

659
00:51:09,462 --> 00:51:10,922
Hey, wait. Let go of me.

660
00:51:11,006 --> 00:51:13,800
Come on, I'm not done talking.

661
00:51:14,634 --> 00:51:17,637
Seriously, let go of me!

662
00:51:17,721 --> 00:51:20,557
If you just come and apologize,
what does that make me?

663
00:51:20,640 --> 00:51:23,894
If you say you'll pay for the damage,
that means I did wrong!

664
00:51:23,977 --> 00:51:27,314
Should I have just let them bad-mouth you?
Better to settle it quickly.

665
00:51:27,814 --> 00:51:31,568
It's not about settling things.
It's about getting the facts straight.

666
00:51:35,238 --> 00:51:37,115
You trust me less than a shaman?

667
00:51:37,199 --> 00:51:38,533
Yes.

668
00:51:39,826 --> 00:51:43,288
-I wouldn't have gone if I didn't have to.
-Why is it so hard to believe me?

669
00:51:43,872 --> 00:51:45,624
Is it so hard to accept that we dated?

670
00:51:45,707 --> 00:51:47,000
-It is.
-Why?

671
00:51:49,336 --> 00:51:52,589
First things first.
You're not the type of guy I'd fall for.

672
00:51:55,967 --> 00:51:56,801
What is your type?

673
00:51:56,885 --> 00:51:57,802
Cha Eun-woo.

674
00:52:00,555 --> 00:52:01,389
Oh, come on.

675
00:52:01,473 --> 00:52:03,433
At the very least,

676
00:52:03,516 --> 00:52:05,435
you're not my type.

677
00:52:06,436 --> 00:52:09,231
And second, your kiss was too clumsy.

678
00:52:10,023 --> 00:52:12,525
You don't kiss like that
after two years together.

679
00:52:12,609 --> 00:52:13,610
And third,

680
00:52:15,195 --> 00:52:16,905
you're not warm.

681
00:52:18,907 --> 00:52:20,784
I went to the gym earlier.

682
00:52:20,867 --> 00:52:24,162
I could tell right away with the Hongs
that they're madly in love.

683
00:52:25,121 --> 00:52:27,999
The term "heart eyes" isn't just a saying.

684
00:52:28,083 --> 00:52:31,962
When you're truly in love,
you can't hide it. The eyes give it away.

685
00:52:32,462 --> 00:52:33,588
But

686
00:52:34,965 --> 00:52:37,717
your eyes are cold.

687
00:52:38,510 --> 00:52:40,428
I can't read your thoughts from your eyes,

688
00:52:40,512 --> 00:52:42,639
let alone your feelings for me.

689
00:52:45,600 --> 00:52:49,479
That's the ultimate reason
I don't believe you, Mr. Jang Tae-ha.

690
00:52:53,358 --> 00:52:55,735
Some people can't afford
to have their emotions read.

691
00:52:58,446 --> 00:53:00,115
Still going with the cool act?

692
00:53:00,198 --> 00:53:01,491
No one's like that.

693
00:53:22,721 --> 00:53:25,348
-I knew this would happen.
-What should we do?

694
00:53:26,891 --> 00:53:28,435
What else?

695
00:53:29,019 --> 00:53:30,645
Go and get me another pair.

696
00:53:30,729 --> 00:53:32,272
And leave you here alone?

697
00:53:32,355 --> 00:53:33,982
No, it's dangerous.

698
00:53:34,065 --> 00:53:36,276
What could be so dangerous
in a country village?

699
00:53:36,359 --> 00:53:38,194
At most, a deer might jump out.

700
00:53:39,070 --> 00:53:39,988
Should I…

701
00:53:43,450 --> 00:53:44,284
carry you?

702
00:53:44,367 --> 00:53:45,994
Don't get clever with me.

703
00:53:47,829 --> 00:53:49,956
You could have gone and come back by now.

704
00:53:59,090 --> 00:54:01,301
Fine. Wait here for a second.

705
00:55:29,431 --> 00:55:30,265
What happened?

706
00:55:32,308 --> 00:55:34,811
What's wrong? Are you okay?

707
00:55:37,564 --> 00:55:39,274
I'm not okay.

708
00:55:40,358 --> 00:55:43,111
I said I'm not okay.

709
00:55:45,071 --> 00:55:50,368
Put yourself in my shoes.
You have no idea how scared I am.

710
00:55:51,202 --> 00:55:54,956
I woke up and couldn't remember a thing.

711
00:55:55,039 --> 00:55:56,624
I'm told I don't have any family,

712
00:55:56,708 --> 00:55:59,377
I don't have any of my friends' numbers,

713
00:55:59,961 --> 00:56:01,546
and my so-called boyfriend

714
00:56:01,629 --> 00:56:05,258
doesn't seem like my boyfriend at all,
no matter how I look at him.

715
00:56:05,758 --> 00:56:08,219
But there's nothing I can do.

716
00:56:08,803 --> 00:56:11,973
I have no money and nowhere to go.

717
00:56:12,932 --> 00:56:14,976
And I don't even have my memory.

718
00:56:20,690 --> 00:56:21,858
See? I told you.

719
00:56:22,358 --> 00:56:26,029
I'm crying like this, but you're just
standing there doing nothing.

720
00:56:26,112 --> 00:56:29,616
What kind of boyfriend does that?

721
00:56:29,699 --> 00:56:33,828
How am I supposed to believe you
when you act like this?

722
00:56:36,498 --> 00:56:38,917
Your eyes are cold.

723
00:56:39,000 --> 00:56:41,127
I can't read your thoughts from your eyes,

724
00:56:41,211 --> 00:56:42,962
let alone your feelings for me.

725
00:56:43,046 --> 00:56:47,091
That's the ultimate reason
I don't believe you, Mr. Jang Tae-ha.

726
00:56:52,138 --> 00:56:53,264
I'll make you believe.

727
00:56:56,184 --> 00:56:57,018
What?

728
00:56:57,602 --> 00:56:58,937
So don't cry.

729
00:57:11,491 --> 00:57:12,992
First, put these on.

730
00:57:33,596 --> 00:57:34,597
Now listen carefully.

731
00:57:38,226 --> 00:57:40,103
I liked you from the moment I saw you.

732
00:57:44,065 --> 00:57:46,693
I wanted to ask for your name and number,

733
00:57:47,944 --> 00:57:49,237
but I couldn't say anything.

734
00:57:49,320 --> 00:57:51,364
I regretted that for a long time…

735
00:57:52,907 --> 00:57:55,201
and I couldn't stop thinking about you.

736
00:57:55,702 --> 00:57:56,953
I just hoped…

737
00:57:59,038 --> 00:58:00,498
to see you again someday.

738
00:58:02,083 --> 00:58:04,335
And I was so happy when we finally met.

739
00:58:06,421 --> 00:58:10,383
Even then, I beat myself up for not having
the courage to tell you how I felt.

740
00:58:12,260 --> 00:58:14,429
I vowed that if we ever met again,

741
00:58:15,054 --> 00:58:17,056
I'd never let you go.

742
00:58:18,099 --> 00:58:20,101
I made that vow over and over again.

743
00:58:22,395 --> 00:58:26,774
Seeing you hurt was unbearable.
It killed me.

744
00:58:27,400 --> 00:58:28,776
If only I could…

745
00:58:32,488 --> 00:58:34,324
I would have killed…

746
00:58:36,451 --> 00:58:38,703
every last soul who did this to you.

747
00:58:44,000 --> 00:58:46,044
I'm sorry I'm not Cha Eun-woo.

748
00:58:49,339 --> 00:58:51,049
And for not expressing myself well.

749
00:58:51,633 --> 00:58:54,052
You're the only woman I've ever liked,

750
00:58:55,470 --> 00:58:57,680
so I don't really know how.

751
00:59:01,184 --> 00:59:02,226
And as for…

752
00:59:04,479 --> 00:59:06,689
the clumsy kiss…

753
00:59:21,120 --> 00:59:23,039
That man is Mayor Ju's aide.

754
00:59:23,122 --> 00:59:26,501
He went undercover
to gather information on the prosecution.

755
00:59:31,756 --> 00:59:33,049
The clumsy kiss…

756
00:59:41,808 --> 00:59:42,642
Forget it.

757
00:59:45,228 --> 00:59:46,187
This one's for real.

758
01:00:14,090 --> 01:00:15,758
OUR STICKY LOVE

759
01:01:02,388 --> 01:01:06,350
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi

